        "notes": "verdict=major-revision. referee_argument: The proof's terminal inference is invalid. It legitimately establishes algebra-level orthogonality (Pythagoras: ||alpha||^2 = ||tau_hat alpha||^2 + ||alpha - tau_hat alpha||^2) but then claims, 'by linearity of the categorical trace', the unrelated equality m(rho) = ||tr(tau_hat alpha)|| + ||tr(alpha - tau_hat alpha)|| and writes QED. Linearity of tr only gives tr(alpha) = tr(tau_hat alpha) + tr(alpha - tau_hat alpha) (a sum inside one norm; merely a triangle inequality for the norms), and squared-norm additivity does not survive the trace. A counterexample with anti-parallel trace images gives LHS 0 vs RHS positive. The Lean leaves this `sorry`, so the formalization neither corroborates the QED nor catches the gap."
